From 2b1cf47616964c5fb4da66f176955317a19347d8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?St=C3=A9phane=20Graber?= <stgraber@stgraber.org>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 07:44:58 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] incusd/instance/qemu: Take the VM disk format from config at
 startup

The metadata image helper read the format from the disk's own bytes, so
a guest that wrote a qcow2 header into its raw root disk had that header
honoured at the next start, letting it name a host path as a backing or
external data file.

Take the format from the volume config, as the publish and NBD paths
already do, and force the raw format when reading a raw volume's size.

This addresses GHSA-4375-qwr5-8vjj (CVE pending)

(cherry picked from commit 06e7033baabd01146093985152e0f7d9bb3470e7)
